\layout Qupart

Explain the difference in the number of staff required in the centralized
 call centre in comparison to the three original call centres.
 In your answer you should focus on the utilization factors in the two systems.
\begin_deeper 
\layout Mypercent

20
\end_deeper 
\layout Standard


\begin_inset ERT
status Collapsed

\layout Standard

\backslash 
answer{
\end_inset 


\layout Subsection*

Answer
\layout Standard

The centralized system requires 9 fewer staff than the original three separate
 systems for approximately the same performance.
 The reason for this improved performance is the improved efficiency of
 the system.
 In the original system the average efficiency can be found from the utilization
 factors.
\layout Itemize

Region X: 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho_{X}=\frac{\lambda}{m}\tau=\frac{50\times6}{12\times60}=\frac{5}{12}$
\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

Region Y: 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho_{Y}=\frac{\lambda}{m}\tau=\frac{70\times6}{15\times60}=\frac{7}{15}$
\end_inset 


\layout Itemize

Region Z: 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho_{Z}=\frac{\lambda}{m}\tau=\frac{25\times6}{8\times60}=\frac{5}{16}$
\end_inset 


\layout Standard

so the average efficiency is 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{1}{3}\left(\frac{5}{12}+\frac{7}{15}+\frac{5}{16}\right)=0.399$
\end_inset 


\newline 
For the centralised system 
\begin_inset Formula $m=26,$
\end_inset 

 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda=50+70+25=145$
\end_inset 

 (by superposition of Poissons), and 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau=0.1$
\end_inset 

.
 So efficiency is
\begin_inset Formula \[
\rho=\frac{\lambda\tau}{m}=\frac{145\times0.1}{26}=0.557.\]

\end_inset 

The second system is therfore more efficient which explains the reduction
 in numbers of staff required.
\layout Standard


\series bold 
\emph on 
10 for the basic answer (i.e.
 the improved efficiency of the system) and 10 for the actual figures.
